{c: Structure Reference}
Intro×2, V1, PC1, C1, C2, Rf, V2, PC2, C1, C2, Rf×2, B×4, C1, C2, Outro, E
(Chorus appears as two distinct sub-sections, C1 and C2, each with different chords on the "Eu... me alegrarei" line — they are NOT duplicates of each other and are both written in full. The C1/C2 pair itself repeats 3 times per the structure above [after PC1, after PC2, and again before Outro] with identical lyrics and chords each time, per the source chart, so only the first occurrence is written in full. Refrain "Oh, oh" repeats 3 times total [Rf, then Rf×2] — same treatment. Bridge chart shows one 4-line pass; song structure calls for it x4 — chord voicings for additional passes beyond what's notated on the chart weren't provided, so only the single documented pass is included.)
